---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const cards = [
  { id: 'boat-day', num: '01', img: '/images/itinerary/kleftiko-boat.jpg', alt: 'A private boat anchored in clear water off Milos',
    h: 'Your day on the water', tag: 'Kleftiko is the reason you came', meta: 'Booked · the first thing I hold on Milos',
    desc: 'Volcanic rock and impossible water &mdash; Milos looks like nowhere else in Greece, and it&rsquo;s best seen from a boat. Kleftiko&rsquo;s sculpted white cliffs, the sea caves, and the swim stops along the western coastline that no road reaches: this is the day the whole trip is built around, and I charter it privately with Salty Rides, my preferred boat partner on the island, rather than through a booking site.',
    notes: [
      ['Kleftiko.', 'The island&rsquo;s most unforgettable day on the water &mdash; white cliffs carved into arches and caves, and water so clear the boat looks like it&rsquo;s floating on air. Only reachable by sea.'],
      ['The western coastline.', 'Skinopi and Er&#275;ma are perfectly positioned for it: book the boat for the next morning and see the western coast before the crowds arrive.'],
      ['Sarakiniko first.', 'On the boat day I&rsquo;d set out early for Sarakiniko&rsquo;s lunar landscape before boarding &mdash; it&rsquo;s the encore, and it&rsquo;s empty at sunrise and full by ten.'],
      ['Private over shared, always.', 'A private boat is the day at your pace &mdash; the swim stops, the lunch, and the light. I&rsquo;ll match the boat to your budget rather than the other way around.'],
      ['The wind decides.', 'The Meltemi can move a boat day with little notice, so I place it early in your stay with room to shift it &mdash; which you can&rsquo;t do once you&rsquo;ve prepaid a fixed date online.'],
    ],
    take: 'If seeing an island from the water is the reason you booked Milos, this is the booking that has to happen first. Send me your dates and I&rsquo;ll hold the boat before the good mornings are gone.' },
  { id: 'restaurants', num: '02', img: '/images/hotels/skinopi-2.jpg', alt: 'Breakfast on the terrace at Skinopi Lodge, Milos',
    h: 'Dinner reservations', tag: 'A handful of tables, and a village to walk to', meta: 'Booked · 2–4 weeks ahead in high season',
    desc: 'Milos eats simpler than Paros &mdash; grilled fish, a table at the water&rsquo;s edge, a village to wander afterward &mdash; and that&rsquo;s the point. But the handful of places worth planning an evening around are small, and in July and August the waterfront tables at the hour worth having go to the people who booked. Tell me your dates and I&rsquo;ll hold the nights that matter and leave the rest loose.',
    notes: [
      ['Medusa, Mandrakia.', 'Grilled fish above a tiny fishing harbor &mdash; the first dinner I&rsquo;d book on the island, and one of the two tables I hold before you land.'],
      ['Armenaki, Pollonia.', 'The other one. The village&rsquo;s best seafood table, and if you&rsquo;re at White Pebble it&rsquo;s a stroll from your room &mdash; the village is the amenity.'],
      ['O!Hamos, Adamas.', 'The long farewell dinner overlooking the water &mdash; where the last night on Milos should end.'],
      ['Lunch at Alkis, Pollonia.', 'A relaxed waterfront lunch after a swim in Pollonia &mdash; the first afternoon of the trip, as I&rsquo;d plan it.'],
      ['Or stay in.', 'Onero has a signature restaurant and private terrace dining; Skinopi gives you an outdoor kitchen and a breakfast basket on your terrace instead &mdash; on purpose. Some of the best evenings on Milos are the ones where you never leave.'],
    ],
    take: 'Two tables held across a four-night stay, and let the rest be long lunches. Send me your dates and I&rsquo;ll tell you which nights are already tight and what I can still get.' },
  { id: 'beaches', num: '03', img: '/images/islands/milos-days.jpg', alt: 'The path down to a hidden cove on Milos', imgStyle: 'object-position:center 45%;',
    h: 'Beaches &amp; the car', tag: 'Rent the car. Then leave the plan loose.', meta: 'Best for · beach lovers, adventure travelers, anyone who&rsquo;d rather find the cove themselves',
    desc: 'Every beach on Milos looks different &mdash; volcanic cliffs, white rock, hidden coves &mdash; and the best of them are spread across the coastline at the end of dirt tracks. A car or ATV isn&rsquo;t optional here; it&rsquo;s the trip. I&rsquo;ll have it waiting when you land. What you do with it is the part worth leaving unplanned.',
    notes: [
      ['Sarakiniko at sunrise.', 'The iconic lunar landscape before the crowds arrive. Go once at dawn and you&rsquo;ll understand why every photo of Milos is this beach.'],
      ['The western beaches by ATV.', 'Remote coves and dramatic coastline that are difficult to reach any other way &mdash; the half of the island most visitors never see.'],
      ['A swim in Pollonia.', 'The easy afternoon: swim, a waterfront lunch at Alkis, a wander through the village, and sunset cocktails overlooking the Aegean.'],
      ['Kimolos, for a day or a night.', 'The ferry leaves from Pollonia, and it&rsquo;s one of the easiest day trips in the Cyclades &mdash; stay in a traditional boat house if you want one of the most authentic nights in the islands.'],
    ],
    take: 'Milos rewards curiosity. Leave time to turn down roads you hadn&rsquo;t planned to take &mdash; you&rsquo;ll often discover your favorite beach by accident. I&rsquo;ll book what needs booking and leave the afternoons alone.' },
];
---
<Layout
  canonical="already-booked-milos.html"
  title="Already Booked Milos? Start Here | Suites With Keith"
  description="Send me the booking details for the hotel you already reserved. I'll have my perks added — no changes to your reservation — and build the rest of the trip around it: the Kleftiko boat day, the car, the tables, the ferries."
  preload="/images/islands/milos-hero.jpg"
>

<!-- hero -->
<header class="hero" style="min-height:min(76svh,700px);">
  <img class="hero-img" src="/images/islands/milos-hero.jpg" alt="The white rock of Sarakiniko, Milos" width="1350" height="1800" fetchpriority="high" />
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Milos &middot; already booked</p>
    <h1 class="display-xl" style="margin-top:18px;">Already booked<br><em>your hotel?</em></h1>
    <p class="sub">Send me the booking details for the hotel you already reserved. I&rsquo;ll have my perks added &mdash; no changes to your reservation &mdash; and then I&rsquo;ll build the rest of the trip around it: the Kleftiko boat day, the car, the tables, the ferries.</p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a class="btn" href="#inquire" data-gtag-label="send_reservations" data-gtag-location="hero">Send me your booking details</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- intro -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container ab-intro">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="deck" style="max-width:46ch;">Keep the room you booked. Send me the confirmation, and I&rsquo;ll add my perks to it and build the rest of Milos around it.</p>
      <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:20px; max-width:58ch;">First, the part most people don&rsquo;t know: you don&rsquo;t have to have booked through me to get my perks. Send me the booking details for the hotel you already reserved and I&rsquo;ll have them added &mdash; a space-available upgrade, daily breakfast, a hotel credit, whatever the property extends to my clients &mdash; with no changes to your existing reservation. Same room, same dates, same rate.</p>
      <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:14px; max-width:58ch;">Then the real work starts, because on Milos the boat day isn&rsquo;t an excursion &mdash; it&rsquo;s the island. You experience Milos from the water or you miss it, and the good boats on the good mornings go first. The rest is a car, a handful of tables in villages where the restaurant is the point, and ferries that behave in September and not always in August. That&rsquo;s the part I take on too. With your confirmation and your dates I&rsquo;ll come back with a plan for the days around it &mdash; a private boat to Kleftiko on the right morning, the car waiting when you land, the tables worth holding held, and transfers that account for what the Aegean does in high season.</p>
      <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:14px; max-width:58ch;">Milos has long been the island my clients ask about most, and I spent my time there the way I&rsquo;d want you to &mdash; on the water, on the dirt roads to the western beaches, and in Pollonia after dark. None of this comes off a list. Still deciding on the hotel? Start with my <a href="/milos.html" style="color:var(--brass);">Milos guide</a> or <a href="/paros-vs-milos.html" style="color:var(--brass);">Paros or Milos?</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal" style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px;">
      <p class="stamp plain" style="font-weight:700; color:var(--brass);">How it works</p>
      <div style="margin-bottom:22px;">
        <p class="ab-note"><b>01 &middot; Send me the booking details</b> <span>for the hotel you&rsquo;ve already reserved &mdash; or just forward the confirmation email.</span></p>
        <p class="ab-note"><b>02 &middot; I have my perks added.</b> <span>No changes to your existing reservation &mdash; same room, same dates, same rate.</span></p>
        <p class="ab-note"><b>03 &middot; I build the rest of the trip around it.</b> <span>Everything below.</span></p>
      </div>
      <p class="stamp plain" style="font-weight:700; color:var(--brass);">What I handle</p>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#inquire"><b>Send me your booking details &rarr;</b></a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#boat-day">Your day on the water</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#restaurants">Dinner reservations</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#beaches">Beaches &amp; the car</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#villages">The villages evening</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#athens">Athens add-on</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#extensions">Santorini &amp; Paros extensions</a>
      <a class="toc-link" href="#logistics">Transfers &amp; ferries</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{cards.map((c, i) => (
  <section class={`section${i % 2 === 0 ? ' band on-shadow' : ''}`} id={c.id} style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class={`ab-grid${i % 2 ? ' flip' : ''}`}>
        <figure class="reveal ab-media">
          <img src={c.img} alt={c.alt} width="1800" height="1300" loading={i === 0 ? 'eager' : 'lazy'} decoding="async" style={c.imgStyle} />
        </figure>
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="stamp plain" style={`font-weight:700; color:${i % 2 === 0 ? 'var(--brass-lit)' : 'var(--brass)'};`}>No. {c.num}</span>
          <h2 class="display-l" style="margin-top:12px;" set:html={c.h} />
          <p class="deck" style="margin-top:10px; font-size:1.05rem;" set:html={c.tag} />
          <p class="stamp plain ab-meta" set:html={c.meta} />
          <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:18px;" set:html={c.desc} />
          <div style="margin-top:22px;">
            {c.notes.map(([b, t]) => <p class="ab-note"><b set:html={b} /> <span set:html={t} /></p>)}
          </div>
          <div class="verdict" style="margin-top:26px;"><p class="ab-take" set:html={c.take} /></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
))}

<!-- easiest way to start -->
<section class="section" style="padding:64px 0;">
  <div class="container ab-callout reveal">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow" style="display:block; margin-bottom:12px;">The easiest way to start</span>
      <h3 class="display-m">Send me your booking details</h3>
      <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:12px; max-width:52ch;">Your hotel confirmation and your dates are enough. I&rsquo;ll have my perks added to the reservation you already have &mdash; nothing about it changes &mdash; and come back with what I&rsquo;d book around it, and what&rsquo;s already getting tight on your nights.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn" href="#inquire">Send your booking details</a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- the villages evening -->
<section class="section band on-shadow" id="villages" style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">The villages evening</span>
      <h2 class="display-l">Plaka, Klima, and dinner on the water</h2>
      <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:16px; max-width:62ch;">Milos&rsquo; villages are small, close together, and at their best in the last two hours of light. This is the evening I&rsquo;d build once &mdash; in the right order, with the table held.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ab-wine">
      <figure class="reveal" style="margin:0;">
        <img src="/images/itinerary/milos.jpg" alt="A fishing boat off the coast of Milos" width="1467" height="2200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="width:100%; aspect-ratio:4/5; object-fit:cover;" />
      </figure>
      <div class="ledger reveal" style="border-top:1px solid var(--band-hairline);">
        <div class="ledger-row"><span class="n">01</span><span class="d"><b>Plaka, late afternoon.</b> The hilltop village &mdash; local boutiques, authentic tavernas, and the island&rsquo;s best sunset views. Wander the lanes before the light goes. <span class="ab-wmeta">Sunset from the hilltop &middot; around 6:30pm</span></span></div>
        <div class="ledger-row"><span class="n">02</span><span class="d"><b>Down to Klima.</b> A few minutes below Plaka: the colorful fishermen&rsquo;s houses at the water&rsquo;s edge, and the postcard everyone comes for. If you&rsquo;re at Skinopi it&rsquo;s practically your neighborhood. <span class="ab-wmeta">Fishermen&rsquo;s houses &middot; golden hour</span></span></div>
        <div class="ledger-row"><span class="n">03</span><span class="d"><b>Dinner overlooking the water.</b> Medusa in Mandrakia or O!Hamos in Adamas &mdash; both a short drive, both tables I hold before you land. <span class="ab-wmeta">Booked ahead &middot; around 9:00pm</span></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="verdict reveal" style="margin-top:40px; max-width:640px; border-left-color:var(--brass-lit);">
      <p>Milos is small enough that this whole evening happens within twenty minutes of your hotel. I hold the table and put it on a night that doesn&rsquo;t follow the boat day, so nobody is rushing back from the water to make it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- athens add-on -->
<section class="section" id="athens" style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="ab-grid">
      <figure class="reveal ab-media">
        <img src="/images/islands/athens-hero.jpg" alt="Athens at dusk" width="1800" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </figure>
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="stamp plain" style="font-weight:700; color:var(--brass);">No. 04</span>
        <h2 class="display-l" style="margin-top:12px;">The Athens add-on</h2>
        <p class="deck" style="margin-top:10px; font-size:1.05rem;">Two or three nights, not a layover</p>
        <p class="stamp plain ab-meta">Best for · bookending the trip, food lovers, first-time Greece</p>
        <p class="body-2" style="margin-top:18px;">Most people treat Athens as a gateway to the islands. I think that&rsquo;s a mistake. Give yourself two or three nights and you&rsquo;ll discover one of Europe&rsquo;s most exciting food cities, incredible luxury hotels, and neighborhoods that feel completely different from one another. It&rsquo;s the perfect way to begin or end a trip through Greece.</p>
        <div style="margin-top:22px;">
          <p class="ab-note"><b>Put it at the end, not the beginning.</b> <span>Flying home out of Athens gives you a buffer against a cancelled ferry or a delayed island flight &mdash; and you arrive in the city already unwound.</span></p>
          <p class="ab-note"><b>Two nights is the minimum that works.</b> <span>One night is an airport hotel with extra steps. Three is genuinely great.</span></p>
          <p class="ab-note"><b>Book the Acropolis early.</b> <span>Timed entry, and the first slot of the morning is the only one worth having in summer.</span></p>
        </div>
        <div class="verdict" style="margin-top:26px;"><p class="ab-take">Read the full <a href="/athens.html">Athens guide</a> for where I&rsquo;d stay and how I&rsquo;d spend the days.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- extensions -->
<section class="section" id="extensions" style="padding-top:0; scroll-margin-top:70px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Santorini &amp; Paros extensions</span>
      <h2 class="display-l">Add one island, not three</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="cards reveal" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr)); max-width:760px;">
      <a class="card" href="/santorini.html">
        <img src="/images/islands/santorini-hero.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="object-position:center bottom;" />
        <div class="pad"><span class="kicker">The Cyclades</span><h3>Santorini</h3><p>The classic finale &mdash; Milos first for the water, then the caldera. Roughly two hours by high-speed boat, or a helicopter.</p><span class="go">Read the guide &rarr;</span></div>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/paros.html">
        <img src="/images/islands/paros-hero.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <div class="pad"><span class="kicker">The Cyclades</span><h3>Paros</h3><p>The eating island &mdash; Naousa on foot at night, and Cosme and Par&imacr;lio, the sister hotels to Er&#275;ma.</p><span class="go">Read the guide &rarr;</span></div>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="verdict reveal" style="margin-top:36px; max-width:640px;">
      <p>Milos is three to four nights for most people. Milos then Santorini is the swimming trip on my <a href="/greek-island-pairings.html" style="color:var(--brass);">pairings page</a>; Paros then Milos is the one I&rsquo;d build for the table and the water in one week. And if you&rsquo;d rather skip Santorini entirely, Sifnos is next door and most crossings run under two hours &mdash; <a href="/milos-vs-sifnos.html" style="color:var(--brass);">the pair I keep going back to myself</a>. Two islands per week, whichever two, and I can arrange a private boat or helicopter between them if the ferry schedules don&rsquo;t cooperate.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- logistics -->
<section class="section band on-shadow" id="logistics" style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
  <div class="container ab-log">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-head" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
        <span class="eyebrow">Getting there &amp; around</span>
        <h2 class="display-l" style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,2.8vw,2.2rem);">Airport &amp; ferry logistics</h2>
      </div>
      <dl class="kv">
        <div class="kv-row ab-row"><dt style="color:var(--band-ash);">Arriving</dt><dd style="color:var(--band-ink);">Fly Athens &rarr; MLO, a small airport served from Athens &middot; ferry into Adamas &middot; private boat transfer &middot; private helicopter</dd></div>
        <div class="kv-row ab-row"><dt style="color:var(--band-ash);">Getting around</dt><dd style="color:var(--band-ink);">Rental car or ATV, essential &middot; private transfers &middot; the Kimolos ferry from Pollonia</dd></div>
        <div class="kv-row ab-row"><dt style="color:var(--band-ash);">What I arrange</dt><dd style="color:var(--band-ink);">Private transfers between the airport, Adamas port and your hotel, the car, and the boat days with Salty Rides &mdash; plus private boat transfers and helicopters through my <a href="/hoper.html" style="color:var(--brass-lit);">Hoper partnership</a> for connecting Milos with the rest of the Cyclades.</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <div style="margin-top:20px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:10px;">
        <a class="toc-link" style="color:var(--brass-lit);" href="/greek-ferry-rules.html">5 Greek ferry rules every couple should know &rarr;</a>
        <a class="toc-link" style="color:var(--brass-lit);" href="/milos.html">The Milos guide &rarr;</a>
        <a class="toc-link" style="color:var(--brass-lit);" href="/private-boat-transfers.html">Private boat transfers between islands &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="stamp plain" style="font-weight:700; color:var(--brass-lit); margin-bottom:16px;">Rules I&rsquo;d give any client</p>
      <div class="ab-rule"><b>Never book the last ferry of the day.</b> If it cancels, there&rsquo;s nothing behind it.</div>
      <div class="ab-rule"><b>Put the boat day early in the stay.</b> If the wind moves it, you still have days to move it to.</div>
      <div class="ab-rule"><b>Don&rsquo;t fly home the same day you sail.</b> Build in a night. The Aegean does not care about your itinerary.</div>
      <div class="ab-rule"><b>Two islands per week. That&rsquo;s the limit.</b> Three islands in seven nights is three travel days.</div>
      <div class="verdict" style="margin-top:30px; border-left-color:var(--brass-lit);">
        <p>You&rsquo;ve done the hard part by choosing the hotel. Send me the confirmation, keep the reservation exactly as it is, and let me handle the rest of it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- the form -->
<section class="section inquire" id="inquire" style="scroll-margin-top:70px;">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow reveal" style="display:block; margin-bottom:16px;">Send me your booking details</span>
    <h2 class="display-l reveal">Your confirmation and dates are enough to start</h2>
    <p class="deck reveal" style="margin:18px auto 0; max-width:38ch;">I&rsquo;ll add my perks and build the rest.</p>
    <form class="inquire-form reveal" action="https://formspree.io/f/mjgnadov" method="POST" style="max-width:520px;">
      <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="Already Booked Milos — reservation details" />
      <input type="hidden" name="page" value="already-booked-milos" />
      <input type="text" name="_gotcha" style="display:none" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
      <label for="ab-name">Name</label>
      <input id="ab-name" type="text" name="name" required autocomplete="name" />
      <label for="ab-email">Email</label>
      <input id="ab-email" type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" />
      <label for="ab-hotel">Hotel you booked</label>
      <input id="ab-hotel" type="text" name="hotel" placeholder="Er&#275;ma" autocomplete="off" />
      <label for="ab-dates">Travel dates</label>
      <input id="ab-dates" type="text" name="travel_dates" placeholder="June 2027, 4 nights" autocomplete="off" />
      <label for="ab-details">Confirmation number, and anything else &mdash; rough is fine</label>
      <input id="ab-details" type="text" name="details" placeholder="Conf. 4821XX &middot; honeymoon &middot; want the Kleftiko boat day" autocomplete="off" />
      <button type="submit" class="btn">Send my booking details</button>
      <p class="note">Rather just forward the confirmation email? Send it to keith.pence@fora.travel &mdash; that&rsquo;s the fastest way to get the perks added.</p>
      <p class="status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </form>
    <p class="small reveal" style="margin-top:26px; color:var(--ash);">Nothing about your reservation changes &mdash; same room, same dates, same rate. The perks and the planning are on top. Haven&rsquo;t locked in the hotel yet? Start with <a href="/milos.html" style="color:var(--brass);">the Milos guide</a> &mdash; Skinopi, Er&#275;ma, Onero and White Pebble, and which one fits.</p>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>

<style>
  .toc-link { font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--brass); text-decoration: none; }
  .toc-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .ab-intro { display: grid; gap: 44px; grid-template-columns: 1fr; align-items: start; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .ab-intro { grid-template-columns: 1.5fr 1fr; gap: 80px; } }

  .ab-grid { display: grid; gap: 40px; grid-template-columns: 1fr; align-items: start; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .ab-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.15fr; gap: 64px; }
    .ab-grid.flip .ab-media { order: 2; }
    .ab-media { position: sticky; top: 84px; }
  }
  .ab-grid > * { min-width: 0; }
  .ab-media { margin: 0; }
  .ab-media img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 4/3; object-fit: cover; }
  .ab-meta { display: block; margin-top: 14px; font-size: .64rem; font-weight: 700 !important; }
  .band .ab-meta { color: var(--band-ash); }
  .ab-note { font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.65; margin-bottom: 13px; padding-left: 16px; position: relative; color: var(--ash); }
  .band .ab-note { color: var(--band-ash); }
  .ab-note::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: .62em; width: 4px; height: 4px; background: var(--brass); }
  .band .ab-note::before { background: var(--brass-lit); }
  .ab-note b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }
  .band .ab-note b { color: var(--band-ink); }
